ing proteins is specifically required for cytokinesis</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>133</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>1321</fpage><lpage>1329</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8682867</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Lehner1992"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lehner</surname><given-names>C.F.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The <italic>pebble</italic> gene is required for cytokinesis in <italic>Drosophila</italic></article-title><source>J. Cell Sci.</source><volume>103</volume><year>1992</year><fpage>1021</fpage><lpage>1030</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1487486</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Lorenzietal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lorenzi</surname><given-names>M.V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Castagnino</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Q.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hori</surname><given-names>Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Miki</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distinct expression patterns and transforming properties of multiple isoforms of Ost, an exchange factor for RhoA and Cdc42</article-title><source>Oncogene.</source><volume>18</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>4742</fpage><lpage>4755</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10467422</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Mabuchietal1993"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mabuchi</surname><given-names>I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamaguchi</surname><given-names>Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujimoto</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Morii</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mishima</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Narumiya</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name></person-group><articl